<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martino della Torre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1263">1263</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martino della Torre was a Milanese nobleman and leader of the popular party who in 1259 was made lord of the people of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, beginning the transformation of the commune into a lordship. His family, the della Torre, dominated Milan until 1277, when Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottone-visconti">Ottone Visconti</a> defeated them at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-desio">Battle of Desio</a>, opening the way to Visconti rule.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1259 <b>Martino della Torre</b> was made lord of the people, and the commune gave way to the Lordship of Milan, later dominated by the Visconti.</blockquote><a href="/state/commune-of-milan">Commune of Milan</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1259 <b>Martino della Torre</b> was made lord of the people, turning the Commune of Milan into a lordship.</blockquote><a href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Lodi, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.32,9.5&amp;year=1253" aria-label="Lodi on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: the place of death of Martino della Torre"><image href="/maps/globes/g000n60.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5569 6201h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5569 6201h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=45.32,9.5&amp;year=1253">What was here in 1253? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
